                        <extracts>"By this expression it is supposed," continues / Keating, "that Niall of the Nine Hostages waged war / against Britain or Wales, and perhaps made a conquest / of the country; <i>and it is more than probable</i> that, when the / Irish prince had finished his design upon the kingdom / of Wales, he carried his arms in a fleet to France and / invaded the country at the time called Armorica, but / now Little Brittany, and from thence he led St. Patrick / and his two sisters into captivity.</extracts>
